{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification","id":800719,"title":"Purviews: any significant modification?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T13:51:24-08:00","id":800719,"title":"Purviews: any significant modification?","content":"So,are the Purviews roughly the same, or are they going to be upgraded? Because, to be honest, I thought they were rather bland and not that &quot;divine&quot; until you hit the Ultimate level. Epic Attributes seemed so much more impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:14:21-08:00","id":800789,"title":"","content":"You didn't think conjuring tsunamis, creating life, raining fireballs or having a palace in outer space (Star 9) was very divine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-04-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T18:38:48-08:00","id":800866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification#post800719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So,are the Purviews roughly the same, or are they going to be upgraded? Because, to be honest, I thought they were rather bland and not that &quot;divine&quot; until you hit the Ultimate level. Epic Attributes seemed so much more impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>They will be changed heavily. It's probably the biggest change in a huge sea of system and setting changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T19:22:18-08:00","id":800878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=800789#post800789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't think conjuring tsunamis, creating life, raining fireballs or having a palace in outer space (Star 9) was very divine?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I didn't think was godly was how there appeared to be <i>one thing</i> that you could do at each dot. I wasn't necessarily looking for Mage Spheres, but a <i>touch</i> more flexibility at higher levels might have been more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T22:09:07-08:00","id":801029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=800878#post800878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What I didn't think was godly was how there appeared to be <i>one thing</i> that you could do at each dot. I wasn't necessarily looking for Mage Spheres, but a <i>touch</i> more flexibility at higher levels might have been more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They weren't though. There were multiple Boons for several dots and I believe the possibility for making your own too.<br /> <br /> For example, the following are multiple Fire boons of the same level.<br /> <br /> <br /> Level 4 - Flamin' Bullets<br /> <br /> Level 4 - Blazing Weapon<br /> <br /> Level 9 - Ifrit<br /> <br /> Level 9 - Hotter Than Hot<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------<br /> <br /> Then you have War<br /> <br /> <br /> Three level 4's (Battle Map, Fury of War, Riastrad)<br /> <br /> Two level 5's (Morale Failure, Mortal Stroke)<br /> <br /> Two level 7's (Siege Juggernaut, Colossus Armor)<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> These are just two purview examples. Heck, the Magic purview has limitless possibilities depending on your imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T00:06:19-08:00","id":801195,"title":"","content":"To be fair, most of those were introduced in supplementary books like Companion or Ragnarok. If you don't have those, then yes, Purviews can appear a bit narrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T10:43:05-08:00","id":801501,"title":"","content":"The general idea was <i>supposed</i> to be that each Purview had dozens and dozens of unwritten Boons. You were <i>supposed</i> to write your own powers. But the books didn't provide meaningful guidance or useful rubrics to do that, so it ended up being a terribly crappy system to model mythology with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T11:21:17-08:00","id":801525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801501#post801501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general idea was <i>supposed</i> to be that each Purview had dozens and dozens of unwritten Boons. You were <i>supposed</i> to write your own powers. But the books didn't provide meaningful guidance or useful rubrics to do that, so it ended up being a terribly crappy system to model mythology with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually sure they were ever really meant to model that; the PSPs don't significantly branch, and a lot of Purviews become all-encompassing at higher levels (see the Animal Purview). But yes, they weren't a good system to model myth with, which is why Purviews in 2e have a very broadly applicable base power and a lot of specific, powerful Boons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:11:58-08:00","id":801622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801525#post801525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not actually sure they were ever really meant to model that; the PSPs don't significantly branch, and a lot of Purviews become all-encompassing at higher levels (see the Animal Purview). But yes, they weren't a good system to model myth with, which is why Purviews in 2e have a very broadly applicable base power and a lot of specific, powerful Boons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm curious as to what will become of the Magic Purview. To be honest, I find it very difficult to come up with ideas for fate manipulation other than what's presented in the book. When I think of the term &quot;magic&quot; I instinctively think of everything the other Purviews are already doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T15:26:22-08:00","id":801633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801622#post801622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to what will become of the Magic Purview. To be honest, I find it very difficult to come up with ideas for fate manipulation other than what's presented in the book. When I think of the term &quot;magic&quot; I instinctively think of everything the other Purviews are already doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the same trouble with one of my players who kept referring to Boons as &quot;Spells&quot; which confused me every time. As for Spells, I usually took Inspiration from what Odin could do or was said to be able to do. Just ask yourself &quot;Could Odin feasibly do this by saying the right words?&quot; and if the answer is Yes, you got yourself a spell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T18:35:57-08:00","id":801718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801195#post801195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, most of those were introduced in supplementary books like Companion or Ragnarok. If you don't have those, then yes, Purviews can appear a bit narrow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I got out of Scion after God because, quite frankly, it was difficult to find someone to RP with, and I was becoming less and less impressed by what I saw.. So no, I didn't know that Purviews were supposed to branch out, and it appears that if they were, they were not properly designed to do so. <br /> <br /> So...here's hoping to much-improved Purviews, because frankly the bar is set pretty low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T22:49:05-08:00","id":801816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801633#post801633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had the same trouble with one of my players who kept referring to Boons as &quot;Spells&quot; which confused me every time. As for Spells, I usually took Inspiration from what Odin could do or was said to be able to do. Just ask yourself &quot;Could Odin feasibly do this by saying the right words?&quot; and if the answer is Yes, you got yourself a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, I'm not too knowledgeable about Norse mythology. I was more interested in Greek mythology growing up. What I know about the Norse, I learned from Marvel, which ARE LIARS!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801718#post801718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And I got out of Scion after God because, quite frankly, it was difficult to find someone to RP with, and I was becoming less and less impressed by what I saw.. So no, I didn't know that Purviews were supposed to branch out, and it appears that if they were, they were not properly designed to do so.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So...here's hoping to much-improved Purviews, because frankly the bar is set pretty low. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Personally, I prefer free-form RPing as it's significantly easier than relying on broken game mechanics and promotes writing experience. That's one reason I picked up the books. I knew the game had a tendency to break down, but still thought it would make for some good inspiration.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-06-2016, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T23:44:48-08:00","id":801860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/800719-purviews-any-significant-modification?p=801622#post801622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to what will become of the Magic Purview. To be honest, I find it very difficult to come up with ideas for fate manipulation other than what's presented in the book. When I think of the term &quot;magic&quot; I instinctively think of everything the other Purviews are already doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoth Neall:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I should note that the Magic Purview is probably going to largely go away in favor of a more holistic focus on cultural magics facilitated by the Pantheon-Specific Purview. Magics in the core of Origins will be handled differently, not always in regard to Fate-only, and will be something that can be expanded upon in later books. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}